{% comment %}
  Renders `true` when collection listings are restricted to in-stock products
  (plp-hide-sold-out): the theme setting is on, this is a collection page, and
  the shop has Search & Discovery's Availability filter enabled. Without that
  filter Shopify ignores `filter.v.availability`, so nothing may be forced.
  Capture it; theme.liquid (redirect) and facets.liquid (hidden facet) share it.
  The setting is compared with `false`, not tested for truth: a theme whose
  settings_data predates the setting has no value for it (nil), and the schema
  default (on) doesn't reach Liquid until someone saves the theme settings.

  Accepts:
  - results: {Object} collection
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  if settings.ob_hide_sold_out != false and template.name == 'collection' and results.filters
    for filter in results.filters
      if filter.param_name == 'filter.v.availability'
        echo 'true'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
